quran[18]{c,v,t}:
  44,1,Ha-Mim.
  44,2,By the Manifest Book.
  44,3,"Indeed, We revealed it on a blessed night. And indeed, We have been warning (humankind against evil)."
  44,4,"On this (night), every wise matter is ordained distinctively,"
  44,5,"as a command from Us. Indeed, We have been sending (messengers),"
  44,6,"as a mercy from your Lord. Indeed, He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing,"
  44,7,"the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them, if only you had sure faith."
  44,8,There is no god except Him. He (alone) gives life and causes death. (He is) your Lord and the Lord of your forefathers.
  44,9,"Nay, they are playing around in doubt."
  44,10,So keep waiting for the Day when the sky brings an evident smoke.
  44,11,That will engulf the people. (They will cry out:) ‘This is a painful punishment.’
  44,12,"‘Our Lord! Remove from us this punishment. Truly, we are believers.’"
  44,13,How could there be a reminder (beneficial for them on that Day) when a clear Messenger had already come to them?
  44,14,But they turned away from him and said: ‘(He is) a tutored madman.’
  44,15,"We may remove the punishment a little, but you will surely revert (to your earlier ways)."
  44,16,"The Day when We will strike (them) with the most terrible blow, We will indeed inflict retribution (upon them)."
  44,17,"Indeed, We tested the people of Pharaoh before them when a noble messenger came to them,"
  44,18,"(saying:) ‘Deliver the servants of Allah (i.e. the Children of Israel) to me. Indeed, I am a trustworthy messenger (sent) to you."
